# Milestone: v0.10.11-channel-and-isA
# Covers: stack-exhausted exception is catchable; caught exception matches
#         Exception.Scheduling type via isA(); message includes location.
# blocked: Exception structured-throw + stack-depth diagnostics (defer-v1.x)
# matrix-row: exceptions-scheduling
#
# Reason:
#   isA() shipped at v0.10.11 (Cluster #17 ratify).  Remaining block is
#   two separate v1.x items: (1) Exception structured-throw wiring —
#   `catch(var s if s.isA(Exception.Scheduling))` requires a named
#   Exception.Scheduling proto instance allocated by OP_THROW; the runtime
#   currently throws diagnostic strings; (2) stack-depth diagnostics —
#   the `echo(s)` output `*** input.u:5.16-18: stack space exhausted`
#   requires source-location tracking in the stack-exhaustion path, which
#   is a separate v1.x diagnostic improvement.  Stack-exhaustion detection
#   is present in the C runtime but the typed exception hierarchy is deferred.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate when Exception structured-throw + stack-depth diagnostics land):
# # function f() { f() } |;
# # try { f() } catch(var s if s.isA(Exception.Scheduling)) { echo(s) };
# # [00000001] *** input.u:5.16-18: stack space exhausted
